"prose": [
{
"from": 241,
"to": 251,
"text": "**The gates:** - a probe that no manifest or lock changed, from the base; - the `--locked` workspace build; - the four crates' unit tests; - the Circle Drawer and virtual-node targets; - the stand companions; - the `a11y` leg (`stand_keyboard`, `stand_accessibility_ids`, `virtual_nodes_as_elements` among its targets); - the `stand-repeat` leg; - the pre-push gate (`fast`), which runs `test_capability_statement`; - the `doc` leg, because step 1 adds a public field with a doc; - the operator's hygiene, push, CI read and windows job-log read."
},
{
"from": 253,
"to": 259,
"text": "**What is absent:** - There is no boot-path touchpoint (no binary's start changes; Circle Drawer stays served by no role), so no smoke   entry. - There is no live leg, and no headful self-verify harness in this project. - There is no `audit` leg: the probe holds every manifest and the lock unchanged. - The coverage leg is not run locally; CI's coverage job reads the floors on the pushed tree, and the CI read asserts   green over it."
},
{
"from": 261,
"to": 262,
"text": "**The controls** are step 11's one-shot runs. The diff moves two OS-conditional sites (step 6), which the CI read and the windows job-log read name."
}
],
